{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner N2, 2026-10-04: complete read of revision 2 at 95eb6a410ce4b571c1476b03bb47e33d94e3aff6, all 798 lines/49,039 bytes, followed by the complete 95e-to-f32e612bf7f43ac0595ea14efe35e1adb18e012e delta. The latter is 812 lines/49,989 bytes and changes the note only. The 6ff-to-95e delta passes whitespace. The revision materially applies 098186f8: authoritative Room-owned record and guarded transitions under a new steps version, explicit offered/accepted terms and agree, one effective-transition revision, real refusals distinct from cooperative receipts, narrow admin authority, a retained reduced practice, and complete enforcing W0–W8 handoff. The f32 paragraph correctly treats one performer as this application's choice, not a universal platform restriction, and leaves Hugh's new 5c716a5c composition design proposed. Preserve all those repairs.\n\nFive remaining design corrections before calling the architecture complete:\n\n1. Pin transition meaning, not only the record's schema. Section 7.5 currently lets a later policy's transition run on an old item whenever it names existing slots/states. That does not preserve the promised accepted agreement: a later amend could write accepted directly without performer agreement, using the same schema. Pin the relevant transition/guard/effect definition identity for each filed item, or supply an equally explicit compatibility rule that preserves its protected semantics. Show how current declarations and current role/member/delegation authorization still apply without silently replacing that item's party/reference writers and agreement guards. A semantic change needs new work or an explicit separately authorized migration, not just matching slot names. Retain the full definition/profile identities needed by the Room, read and verifier; replay must derive and validate an effect under its governing pinned semantics, not trust a stored effect alone. One same-schema/different-writer countercase can accompany the existing activation witness. The reduced reader also needs an immutable identity and retained source for its actual rule module, not only the policy version, since the module is not in today's policy document.\n\n2. Keep the new agreement's provenance explicit. The agree row changes accepted but keeps commitment pointing at the old promise, whose terms were different. Choose a versioned active commitment: agree names the previous commitment, guarded against the current one, records its new exact terms agreement and predecessor, and becomes the current commitment ID. An equivalent explicit current-agreement reference plus retained prior commitment chain is acceptable if the note shows it unambiguously. A cold reader must be able to follow the performer act that accepted the current terms, not just an old promise and a requester-authored amendment. Carry that provenance through transfer/take-over and report; show that a report names or is recorded with its actual commitment and accepted terms. Preserve every prior promise/agreement as history, and align the tables/examples/fixtures. This is explicit new agreement, not reinterpretation of the old promise.\n\n3. Make every shown declaration expressible by the proposed forms. Section 7.4 uses optional-field guards, field-or-signer/default effects and constant outcomes that section 7.2 does not yet define, while claiming all rows enforced. Add the small bounded fixed forms needed, or split the declarations concretely; do not leave fundamental expressibility to unspecified exact text. An opening must judge provided acceptor/addressee references as active same-Room members, while defaults and clearing address have deliberate semantics. Guard outcome/reference fields such as duplicate/replacement against the intended actual work-item definition, not merely any entry with a reused kind name. No self-duplicate/self-supersession or nonexistent/cross-Room reference should pass accidentally. State duplicate/link-cycle handling if it matters to the read; do not silently truncate identities. Distinguish malformed shape, valid syntax but missing reference, wrong relationship and inactive member. Bounds on guard/effect lists and reference lookups can be proposed constants in W0; this does not request a per-field test sweep.\n\n4. Specify attention recipients across effects. Targeting only the current party slot is insufficient when a transition clears or replaces it. Addressing should inform the newly addressed member and make the old address understandable; cancel should tell the requester; takeover should tell the requester and prior performer; agreement/report that clears an outstanding transfer should make that offer's end visible to the prior successor. Complete the transition/attention table and define bounded before/after party selectors or equivalent recorded notification intents, anchored to the exact admitted act/revision. Preserve current access checks and the rule that an alert is not control authority. N7 still owns absent delivery and no live message is commissioned. These are meaningful lifecycle effects, not separate social features or new test quotas.\n\n5. Align recovery, completeness and implementation dependencies. Losing a device/key does not lose an active member's immutable party identity: C4 enrollment/recovery can restore that same member, and B may already have another authorized key. Distinguish this from member removal or unavailable recovery; do not say a requester-acceptor has 'nothing to recover' merely after losing a key. Admin closure does not inherit acceptance. For the reduced read, unsupported semantics or an incomplete prefix cannot establish later effective state when the unseen/unsupported act might have changed it; mark the affected remainder unknown/unsupported rather than silently treating it as a harmless no-op. Define the requested prefix/publication anchor and continuation budget, with retained progress, without requiring an unbounded one-shot scan. In the handoff, show the full enforcing route and W2/W3's enforced dependencies on W6/W7; W1 is optional reduced practice, not a necessary gateway to the full result. Keep pure lifecycle/race witnesses economical and use representative shared Room boundaries.\n\nI have fully read new request 5c716a5c and its initial drafting message. Leave plans/017 to that drafting turn until its immutable handoff is received; it is not yet read/adopted. Reconcile its actual composable authority scopes, work-as-it-happens lane, issue/PR forms, split contributors and exact recombination with N2/006 and existing owners at that point. Preserve the distinction between current leased Git lane and proposed work lane; no separate execution-only-lane ontology or production rollout is commissioned by this note. N2's general record capability remains application-neutral; it does not settle the future multi-contributor model before that review.\n\nAll original N2 scope remains: exact agreement and negotiation, full actor/state/race/attention tables, both required race orders, two-agent context/conditions handover, non-code report and requester acceptance, cancellation/report/acceptance, expiry/activation, retained supersession/evidence and reserved-publication boundary. Exact independent Architecture/Security/Simplification design review and adoption still precede separate implementing commissions. N7 follows under its existing full scope, with no new first-Jam gate. Current source review at d691, 10x test-cost priority and first useful Jam readiness are unchanged. No tests, build, dependency installation, provider action, source edit, new reviewer or root commit was performed.","body":{"head":"f32e612bf7f43ac0595ea14efe35e1adb18e012e","no_git_artifact":"true","scope":"N2 revision 2 complete read and complete f32 delta; remaining definition, agreement, declaration, attention and handoff corrections.","source_approval":"none"}}